d on the com- puters and that (ii) it would not exam- ine or otherwise acquire any informa- tion contained in the software. This section does not prevent an account debtor from protecting by agreement its independent interests that are un- related to the “creation, attachment, or perfection” of a security interest. In Ex- ample 1, moreover, the secured party is not in possession of copies of software by virtue of its security interest or in connection with enforcing its security interest in the debtor’s license of the software. Its possession is incidental to its possession of the computers, in which it has a security interest. Enforc- ing against the secured party a restric- tion relating to the software in no way interferes with its security interest in the computers. . . . § 9–408ARTICLE 9"